commit ffd820c619923f5c8719428913903bfc9bc22b4e
Author: Jaimin Detroja <124363976+JaiminPatel345@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Jun 7 12:23:55 2026 +0530

    feat: launcher-state accessibility service — exact page + drawer detection on One UI
    
    Fixes #10
    Fixes #11
    
    New: LauncherStateService (AccessibilityService) restricted to
    com.sec.android.app.launcher. Reads the One UI page indicator
    ("Page N of M. " contentDescription), classifies home vs. drawer
    surface by ancestor resource-id, and publishes results to
    LauncherState (volatile statics — same process, cross-thread safe).
    
    SphereEngine integration:
    - updatePageVisibility(): a11y is the highest-priority page source
      (after preview guard, before offsets-live, before dead-reckoning).
      Falls through gracefully when service is not enabled or update is
      stale (>5 s) — no wedged states.
    - tap() direct-tap fallback: suppressed when drawer is fresh-open
      (isA11yDrawerOpenFresh). Zoom-based guard kept as fallback.
    - onWallpaperTapCommand: belt-and-suspenders drawer check on GL thread.
    - commitPageSwipe(): skips dead-reckoning counter when drawer is open
      so drawer swipes do not drift the home-page estimate.
    
    Settings (opt-in UX):
    - New "Launcher Integration" PreferenceCategory with
      pref_exact_page_detection Preference; state-dependent title/summary
      refreshed in onResume via AccessibilityManager query.
    - Click → Settings.ACTION_ACCESSIBILITY_SETTINGS (try/catch + Toast).
    
    Manifest: service with BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE permission,
    intent-filter, and meta-data pointing to launcher_state_service.xml.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

